**Step 2 – Determine the dilutive effect of the stock options (treasury‑stock method)**  

- Options outstanding: 200,000  
- Exercise price (EP): \$30  
- Average market price (MP) during the year: \$40  

Incremental shares from the options:

\[
\text{Incremental shares}= \text{Options}\times\frac{MP-EP}{MP}
=200{,}000\times\frac{40-30}{40}
=200{,}000\times0.25
=50{,}000\ \text{shares}
\]

**Step 3 – Compute diluted EPS**

\[
\text{Diluted shares}=220{,}000{,}000+50{,}000=220{,}050{,}000
\]

\[
\text{Diluted EPS}= \frac{569\text{ million}}{220{,}050\text{ thousand}}
= \frac{569}{220.05}
\approx 2.58578\ \text{\$/share}
\]

**Step 4 – Difference between basic and diluted EPS**

\[
\text{Basic EPS} - \text{Diluted EPS}
= 2.58636 - 2.58578
\approx 0.00058\ \text{\$/share}
\]

